WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:06.774
"I have to get to Planet Delkor Space Base," Cozlin thought.

2
00:00:06.775 --> 00:00:10.263
"Someone stole a power crystal!"

3
00:00:10.264 --> 00:00:12.999
Power crystals were very important on Delkor.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.598
Vehicles, spaceships, and homes ran on power crystals.

5
00:00:17.599 --> 00:00:19.339
But it didn't make sense.

6
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.232
Everyone got power crystals for free.

7
00:00:22.233 --> 00:00:26.165
Why would someone steal one?

8
00:00:26.166 --> 00:00:28.391
Cozlin peeked into her classroom.

9
00:00:28.392 --> 00:00:31.221
"I'll be right back, Mr. Jex.

10
00:00:31.222 --> 00:00:37.158
Principal Plip needs me to help him with, um, something."

11
00:00:37.159 --> 00:00:44.371
Mr. Jex was still grading tests. "That's fine."

12
00:00:44.372 --> 00:00:48.466
Cozlin ran outside and shot into the sky.

13
00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:53.598
"Look!" Mert said. "It's Kid Comet!"

14
00:00:53.599 --> 00:00:55.740
The students ran to the window.

15
00:00:55.741 --> 00:00:57.032
"Woo-hoo!"

16
00:00:57.033 --> 00:01:04.386
"Go, Kid Comet!"

17
00:01:04.387 --> 00:01:07.587
Cozlin arrived at Planet Delkor Space Base.

18
00:01:07.588 --> 00:01:09.663
She found Detective Borzon.

19
00:01:09.664 --> 00:01:12.207
He was the lead detective on Delkor.

20
00:01:12.208 --> 00:01:15.287
He was talking to a spaceship pilot.

21
00:01:15.288 --> 00:01:18.770
"Hey, Detective," Cozlin said.

22
00:01:18.771 --> 00:01:21.921
"You can't take flying lessons now.

23
00:01:21.922 --> 00:01:25.623
We have a crime to solve."

24
00:01:25.624 --> 00:01:28.442
Detective Borzon groaned.

25
00:01:28.443 --> 00:01:31.014
"Very funny, Kid Comet.

26
00:01:31.015 --> 00:01:32.996
I'm talking to a witness.

27
00:01:32.997 --> 00:01:38.125
This is Quazz. He saw the crystal thief."

28
00:01:38.126 --> 00:01:41.639
"I still don't understand," Cozlin said.

29
00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:46.039
"Why would someone on Delkor steal a free power crystal?"

30
00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.083
Detective Borzon shrugged.

31
00:01:48.084 --> 00:01:51.071
"Maybe the thief wants more power."

32
00:01:51.072 --> 00:01:54.539
"The thief isn't from Delkor," Quazz said.

33
00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.084
"The thief is an alien."

34
00:01:57.085 --> 00:02:01.161
Detective Borzon's eyes went wide. "What?"

35
00:02:01.162 --> 00:02:05.646
"I was on a mission to find a missing satellite," Quazz said.

36
00:02:05.647 --> 00:02:09.594
"I found it—after it crashed into a space station.

37
00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:14.597
It wasn't a Delkor space station though.

38
00:02:14.598 --> 00:02:20.893
It was an alien space station!"

39
00:02:20.894 --> 00:02:23.733
He turned on a computer.

40
00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:28.356
"Watch this. It's a video I took from my spaceship."

41
00:02:28.357 --> 00:02:32.723
Cozlin and the detective saw the space station and broken satellite pieces.

42
00:02:32.724 --> 00:02:34.781
One piece sparkled.

43
00:02:34.782 --> 00:02:38.811
"That's the satellite's power crystal," Cozlin said.

44
00:02:38.812 --> 00:02:43.303
"Yes. Keep watching," Quazz said.

45
00:02:43.304 --> 00:02:45.737
An alien appeared.

46
00:02:45.738 --> 00:02:48.891
"Whoa!" Cozlin said.

47
00:02:48.892 --> 00:02:52.298
The alien grabbed the crystal.

48
00:02:52.299 --> 00:02:55.272
Then he went back into the space station.

49
00:02:55.273 --> 00:02:57.969
Detective Borzon made a fist.

50
00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.997
"No wonder you called us.

51
00:02:59.998 --> 00:03:02.083
This is a serious crime!"

52
00:03:02.084 --> 00:03:04.241
Quazz nodded.

53
00:03:04.242 --> 00:03:06.749
"Don't worry," Cozlin said.

54
00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:11.374
"I'll find that space station—and our crystal!"

55
00:03:11.375 --> 00:03:16.334
She shot into the sky.

56
00:03:16.335 --> 00:03:20.766
"Wait!" Quazz cried. "Come back!"

57
00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:24.782
Cozlin flew back down. "What's wrong?"

58
00:03:24.783 --> 00:03:29.443
"The crystal isn't on that space station anymore," Quazz said.

59
00:03:29.444 --> 00:03:32.627
"How do you know?" Cozlin asked.

60
00:03:32.628 --> 00:03:39.087
"Every power crystal has a tracking device," Quazz said.

61
00:03:39.088 --> 00:03:41.882
He opened another program on his computer.

62
00:03:41.883 --> 00:03:45.223
"The crystal left the space station earlier today.

63
00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:58.126
Let's see where it is now."

64
00:03:58.127 --> 00:04:05.899
He gulped. "The crystal is on an alien planet!"

